---
import AnimatedHero from "../components/AnimatedHero.astro";
import HomeShell from "../components/HomeShell.astro";
---

<HomeShell
  title="Code review that brings receipts"
  description="Warden gives your agent runtime the ground truth for code review over MCP — detectors, verified advisories, real type definitions — and publishes only what survives gates the model cannot skip."
>
  <main class="home-article">
    <div class="home-topline">
      <a class="home-status" href="https://github.com/99Yash/warden/blob/main/decisions.md" rel="noreferrer">
        <span class="home-status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        More than 50 ADRs, every choice written down
      </a>
      <button class="home-command" type="button" data-copy="warden mcp" aria-label="Copy command: warden mcp">
        <code>warden mcp</code>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="13" height="13" aria-hidden="true">
          <rect x="5.5" y="5.5" width="8" height="8" rx="1.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.3"></rect>
          <path d="M10.5 3.5v-.5A1.5 1.5 0 0 0 9 1.5H4A1.5 1.5 0 0 0 2.5 3v5A1.5 1.5 0 0 0 4 9.5h.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.3"></path>
        </svg>
      </button>
    </div>

    <header>
      <h1 class="home-sr-only">Code review that brings receipts</h1>
      <p class="home-tagline">
        Warden gives your agent the parts of a code review it cannot make up: type errors, lint
        findings, advisories checked against OSV, and real <code>.d.ts</code> signatures. Your agent
        runs the review over MCP. Then Warden's gates decide what gets published. The model never
        gets the last word.
      </p>
    </header>

    <AnimatedHero />

    <section>
      <h2>How a review runs</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>
          <strong>Diff.</strong> Warden resolves the base by merge-base, prunes generated files, and
          stops on unsafe input, such as a symlink that leaves the repo.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Det-priors.</strong> The lane calls <code>run_det_priors</code> first and reads the
          findings page by page, by handle.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Lanes.</strong> The down lane proves invariants. The up lane searches for
          structural drift and is opt-in. <span class="home-tag partial">partial</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Post-pass.</strong> Warden verifies citations, keeps each finding inside its lane's
          file scope, demotes by confidence, and caps volume.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Publish.</strong> Warden emits one stable <code>CommentSet</code>. The scope
          envelope comes from the driver, never from the model.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <aside class="home-callout">
        <p>
          <code>warden review</code> still runs the original in-process loop. It stays the default
          until the parity eval shows that the MCP path matches it. The CI runner is a tracer and
          does not comment on PRs yet.
        </p>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What your agent gets</h2>
      <p>
        <code>warden mcp</code> is a local stdio server. Every result carries a schema version, stays
        under a size bound, and returns a structured reason instead of throwing.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong><code>run_det_priors</code></strong>: TSC, ESLint, npm audit with OSV, duplication,
          security lint, and context selection, as a paged bundle
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong><code>lookup_type_def</code></strong>: library API signatures from the installed
          type definitions
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong><code>search_index</code></strong>: semantic repo search
          <span class="home-tag">next</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Agent runtimes get better at sub-agents, model routing, and permissions with every release.
        None of them ships a detector corpus, verified advisories, or a repo index. So Warden hands
        the loop to the runtime and keeps the parts that have to be right.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Connect</h2>
      <p>Add Warden as a local server in <code>opencode.jsonc</code>. Any MCP client works the same way.</p>
      <pre class="home-code"><code><span class="tok-punct">&#123;</span>
  <span class="tok-key">"mcp"</span><span class="tok-punct">: &#123;</span>
    <span class="tok-key">"servers"</span><span class="tok-punct">: &#123;</span>
      <span class="tok-key">"warden"</span><span class="tok-punct">: &#123;</span>
        <span class="tok-key">"type"</span><span class="tok-punct">:</span> <span class="tok-str">"local"</span><span class="tok-punct">,</span>
        <span class="tok-key">"command"</span><span class="tok-punct">: [</span><span class="tok-str">"warden"</span><span class="tok-punct">,</span> <span class="tok-str">"mcp"</span><span class="tok-punct">]</span>
      <span class="tok-punct">&#125;</span>
    <span class="tok-punct">&#125;</span>
  <span class="tok-punct">&#125;</span>
<span class="tok-punct">&#125;</span></code></pre>
      <p>
        Warden is not on npm yet. Point <code>command</code> at a local checkout.
        <a href="/docs/mcp/" data-astro-prefetch>The MCP docs</a> show the exact form.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What lands in a comment</h2>
      <p>Every Warden comment is a small receipt. It earns the right to interrupt you.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Tier</strong>: Block, Fix, or Consider. Tier 1 is what would block a merge, and it
          always survives the volume cap.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Category</strong>: correctness, security, scalability, and others. This is the
          reading order, not the severity.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Sources</strong>: a path, a line, and a snippet. The post-pass matches the snippet
          before the comment ships.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Degraded</strong>: if a lane or a detector fails, the run says so.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <aside class="receipt" aria-label="Sample comment receipt">
        <div class="receipt-row">
          <span class="receipt-key">tier</span>
          <span class="receipt-val tier-1">1 · Block</span>
        </div>
        <div class="receipt-row">
          <span class="receipt-key">lane</span>
          <span class="receipt-val">down · correctness · 91%</span>
        </div>
        <div class="receipt-row">
          <span class="receipt-key">file</span>
          <span class="receipt-val">src/billing/charge.ts:88</span>
        </div>
        <div class="receipt-row">
          <span class="receipt-key">claim</span>
          <span class="receipt-val">
            <span class="receipt-emph">markPaid</span> runs before the charge result is checked, so a
            declined card still ships the order.
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="receipt-row">
          <span class="receipt-key">source</span>
          <span class="receipt-val">charge.ts:88 · quote verified</span>
        </div>
        <div class="receipt-quote">await markPaid(order.id);</div>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Principles</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Runs in your repo</strong>: no hosted backend. Code goes only to the model provider you choose</li>
        <li><strong>Gates are not tools</strong>: a model can skip a tool call, so verification runs after the model, every time</li>
        <li><strong>Measured</strong>: an eval harness scores recall and precision, and a parity eval decides when the new path becomes the default</li>
        <li><strong>Written down</strong>: ADR-0053 explains this page. Keep the method and the gates, and hand the loop to the runtime.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <nav class="home-links" aria-label="Next steps">
      <a href="/docs/mcp/" data-astro-prefetch>Connect over MCP <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      <a href="/docs/review/" data-astro-prefetch>Read how a review runs <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      <a href="https://github.com/99Yash/warden/blob/main/decisions.md" rel="noreferrer">
        Read the decisions <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
    </nav>
  </main>
</HomeShell>

<script>
  // Copy the command chip. Re-bind after each view transition.
  document.addEventListener("astro:page-load", () => {
    for (const button of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-copy]")) {
      button.addEventListener("click", async () => {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(button.dataset.copy ?? "");
        button.dataset.copied = "true";
        setTimeout(() => delete button.dataset.copied, 1400);
      });
    }
  });
</script>
